### 0 cli total
$ xmd total
--- stdin
flights := $420.00
hotel := $180.50
total := flights + hotel
exit 0
--- stdout
$600.50

### 1 cli tasks | where !done | select {title} --json
$ xmd tasks | where !done | select {title} --json
--- stdin
- [x] book flights
- [ ] pack
- [ ] print tickets
exit 0
--- stdout
[
  {
    "title": "pack"
  },
  {
    "title": "print tickets"
  }
]

### 2 cli trip.x.md total
$ xmd trip.x.md total
exit 0
--- stdout
$600.50

### 3 cli trip.x.md tasks | where !done | count
$ xmd trip.x.md tasks | where !done | count
exit 0
--- stdout
2

### 4 cli --workspace tasks | where !done | count
$ xmd --workspace tasks | where !done | count
exit 0
--- stdout
2

### 5 cli total
$ xmd total
--- stdin

exit 1
--- stderr
xmd: Unknown name 'total'

### 6 cli 
$ xmd 
exit 0
--- stdout
Reactive notes with a typed workspace query API. The default command is a query: name a note or pipe one in.

Usage: xmd [OPTIONS] <QUERY>                (note on stdin)
       xmd [OPTIONS] <FILE> <QUERY>
       xmd [OPTIONS] --workspace <QUERY>
       xmd <COMMAND> ...

Commands:
  lsp      Start the language server over stdin/stdout (for editor integrations)
  query    Query tasks, values, tables, plans, resources and diagnostics
  render   Export a saved note with the language server's colors and inline values
  ast      Inspect syntax nodes, source text and expression trees for one note (JSON)
  graph    Inspect dependencies between values, tasks and checklists in one note (JSON)
  refresh  Explicitly refresh cached resource status and external lookups
  sync     Keep a directory of notes in step with a folder in the web app
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [FILE_OR_QUERY]  A note relative to --root, or the query itself when the note is piped in or --workspace is set
  [QUERY]          A functional expression or collection pipeline; use - for stdin

Options:
      --workspace      Query all indexed notes instead of supplying a positional note file
      --root <ROOT>    [default: .]
      --json           Emit a JSON array, preserving dates, currencies and units
      --jsonl          Emit one JSON value per line
      --on <ON>        Evaluate at local midnight on this date
      --now <NOW>      Freeze the clock and timezone offset using an RFC3339 timestamp
      --fail-on-match  Return exit status 1 if the query returns any rows (useful for diagnostics)
  -h, --help           Print help
  -V, --version        Print version

Examples: cat note.x.md | xmd 'total'
          xmd note.x.md 'tasks | where !done' --json
          xmd --workspace 'filter(tasks, fn(t) => !t.done)' --json
          xmd lsp   # the language server, for editors
Run `xmd query --help` for the query bindings, functions and stages.


### 7 cli left
$ xmd left
--- stdin
left := import("./other.x.md").budget - $200.00
exit 0
--- stdout
$800

### 8 cli query total
$ xmd query total --root <root> --now 2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00
--- stdin
total := $600.50
exit 0
--- stdout
$600.50

### 9 cli q tasks | count --json
$ xmd q tasks | count --json
--- stdin
- [ ] pack
exit 0
--- stdout
[
  1
]

### 10 cli trip.x.md -
$ xmd trip.x.md -
--- stdin
tasks | count
exit 0
--- stdout
3

